        <div>
          <h3 class="text-3xl {{ colors.headingsCustom or colors.headingsDefault }} font-bold mb-4">
            Virtual Sports Set Apart
          </h3>
          <p>
            Technology and digital transformation pushes the way we practice sports. One aspect of sports digitalisation is that it creates <b>new forms of sport</b> and new ways to practice. 
            Labelling these as <i>virtual sports</i> helps to set them apart when the boundaries between traditional sports, <a href="/tags/esports/">esports</a>, and <a href="/tags/exergame/">exergames</a> start to blur.
            Virtual sports differentiate themselves primarily through two fundamental dimensions: <b>physicality</b> and <b>reality</b>.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-outside pl-5 space-y-4 mb-4 text-lg md:text-xl">
            <li>
              <b>Physical movements that mimic sports</b><br>
              Recent advancements in technology allows to <b>digitally capture physical movements extremely accurately and sensitively</b>, for instance with milimeter precision in <a href="/2025/03/24/virtual-sports-an-overview-of-what-exists-and-what-is-possible/">virtual golf</a>. 
              This makes virtual sports different from exergames, where accuracy and sensitivity is lower and the focus is more on playful entertainment or rehabilitation rather than athletic competitions.
              Virtual sports also differ from esports, where  physical movement (e.g. fine-motor controls like manipulating a mouse, keyboard, or controller) is required but not aimed at mimicking an existing sport to fearture competitions.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Physical-Digital Interreality</b><br>
              Unlike pure <a href="/2025/03/24/virtual-sports-an-overview-of-what-exists-and-what-is-possible/">sports simulations</a> that leaves data unaltered and merely displays it on a screen, virtual sports take place within its own digital world. 
              <b>Data from real-world performances (e.g. power) is altered based on events in the digital world (e.g. in-game drafting)</b>, which creates a hybrid physical-digital interreality. 
              This means that the algorithms behind virual sports games transform sport competitons into a blend of physical performance and digital strategy.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-3xl {{ colors.headingsCustom or colors.headingsDefault }} font-bold leading-none mb-4">
            A growing interest in Virtual Sports
          </h3>
          <p>
            Because of Virtual Sports' unique and innovative nature, there is a growing interest in Virtual Sports.
            <b>The mission of this science communication blog and research network is to address this interest.</b>
          </p>
          <p>
            Our aims are (1) to set a name for the Virtual Sports 'label' as a new type of physical and sports-alike (eSports) games, 
            (2) to inform people on the perspectives and debates virtual sports brings to the sports sector and academia, 
            and (3) to connect academics with expertise in virtual sports into a network that is reachable for everyone interested.

          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sticky Media Column -->
